# NEURAL PAIRING: the score.
#
# A 60-second cue for an animated explainer: two glowing creatures (Quill,
# violet; Ember, orange) assemble, find they cannot pass words, grow eight
# bridges between their hidden states, play, train under ice, and prove it.
# Cinematic synthwave with Cliff Martinez glass and a playful bounce, in
# D major. 120 bpm: 1 beat = 0.5 s, 1 bar = 2.0 s, 30 bars = 60.0 s.
# Every cue is pinned to an absolute beat with `>` seeks (beat = 2 x seconds).
#
#   0.0   swell from silence (pad, air)        beat   0
#   0.4   assembly arpeggio, Quill L / Ember R  beats 0.8-6.05
#   3.0   eyes-open chime                       beat   6
#   8.0   SHATTER (crash, shards, boom)         beat  16
#   10.0  THE DROP + 8 rising bridge plucks     beats 20..27
#   14.5  whoosh/dive -> glass mechanism        beats 29..42.4
#   22.0  IMPACT -> playful games               beat  44
#   29.5  "lantern" resolve                      beat  59
#   30.5-32.5 five staccato value-game hits     beats 61..65
#   33-36 bouncy play                           beats 66..72
#   36.0  ticking training                      beat  72
#   40.0  ice shimmer                           beat  80
#   43-46 riser                                 beats 86..92
#   46.0  near-silence                          beat  92
#   48.0  the stranger's sour note              beat  96
#   50.0  BIG HIT, full groove                  beat 100
#   53.0 / 53.8 / 54.6 stat hits                beats 106, 107.6, 109.2
#   55.6  warm anthem outro, fade by 59.9       beats 111.2..120
#
# The noise-only FX (air, risers, whooshes, crash wash, frost, rumble) are
# rendered first from fx.song and played back here on the tape deck.

bpm 120
gate 0.9
tail 2.5

section INTRO   0..16
section RULE    16..20
section LINK    20..29
section GLASS   29..44
section PLAY    44..72
section TRAIN   72..92
section HUSH    92..100
section PROOF   100..111.2
section TITLE   111.2..120

